    "q-170808": {
      "dom_id": "step-q170808",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "$\\,$ $x$ is not positive, or $x$ is not odd.\n\nExpress the compound predicate above in symbolic form given the following predicates:\n\n- $P(x):$ $x$ is positive\n\n- $Q(x):$ $x$ is odd",
      "worked_solution": "Let's break our sentence down into individual statements:\n\n- The sentence \"$x$ is not positive\" can be expressed symbolically as $¬P.$\n\n- The sentence \"$x$ is not odd\" can be expressed symbolically as $¬Q.$\n\nTherefore, the given sentence is expressed symbolically as \n\n$$\n¬P∨¬Q.\n$$",
