      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "$\\,$ $x$ is neither irrational nor complex.\n\nExpress the compound predicate above in symbolic form given the following predicates:\n\n- $S(x):$ $x$ is irrational\n\n- $T(x):$ $x$ is complex",
      "worked_solution": "The given sentence is equivalent to the following sentence: \n\n$\\,$ $x$ is not irrational, and $x$ is not complex.\n\nLet's break our sentence down into individual statements:\n\n- The statement \"$x$ is not irrational\" can be expressed symbolically as $¬S.$\n\n- The statement \"$x$ is not complex\" can be expressed symbolically as $¬T.$\n\nTherefore, the given sentence is expressed symbolically as\n\n$$\n¬S∧¬T.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
