    "q-183269": {
      "dom_id": "step-q183269",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "$\\,$ $x$ is not both a multiple of $5$ and a multiple of $9.$\n\nExpress the compound predicate above in symbolic form given the following predicates:\n\n- $P(x):$ $x$ is a multiple of $5$\n\n- $Q(x):$ $x$ is a multiple of $9$",
      "worked_solution": "The given sentence is the negation of the following sentence: \n\n$\\,$ $x$ is both a multiple of $5$ and a multiple of $9.$\n\nThe sentence above can be expressed symbolically as $P∧Q,$ and we can negate this sentence using the symbol \"$¬$\".\n\nTherefore, the given sentence is expressed symbolically as\n\n$$\n¬(P∧Q).\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
