      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "$\\,$ $a<2\\text{ or }b\\le 1.$\n\nThe negation of the composite predicate above is the following:\n\n$\\,$ \n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}{{field-3}}",
      "worked_solution": "De Morgan's law for disjunctions states that\n\n$$\n¬(A∨B)=¬A∧¬B.\n$$\n\nSo, the negation of \"$a<2\\text{ or }b\\le 1$\" is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(a<2\\text{ or }b\\le 1) & ≡¬(a<2∨b\\le 1) \\\\  & ≡¬(a<2)∧¬(b\\le 1) \\\\  & ≡a\\ge 2∧b>1 \\\\  & ≡a\\ge 2\\text{ and }b>1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
