    "q-183346": {
      "dom_id": "step-q183346",
      "name": "Question 15",
      "problem": "$\\,$ $x=2$ or $y\\ne -2.$\n\nThe negation of the composite predicate above is the following:\n\n$\\,$ \n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}{{field-3}}",
      "worked_solution": "De Morgan's law for disjunctions states that\n\n$$\n¬(A∨B)=¬A∧¬B.\n$$\n\nSo, the negation of \"$x=2$ or $y\\ne -2$\" is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(x=2\\text{ or }y\\ne -2) & ≡¬(x=2∨y\\ne -2) \\\\  & ≡¬(x=2)∧¬(y\\ne -2) \\\\  & ≡x\\ne 2∧y=-2 \\\\  & ≡x\\ne 2\\text{ and }y=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
